        {
          "type": "assignment",
          "title": "Hero's Journey Zine or Comic",
          "href": "https://roundrockisd.schoology.com/assignment/8180639473",
          "assignmentDetails": {
            "score": "105/100",
            "description": "<p style=\"margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:1em;margin-left:0px;padding:0px;line-height:1.4;\" dir=\"ltr\">Select one:</p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li style=\"margin:0px;\">After learning about the hero’s journey, and reading “The Cyclops” from&nbsp;<em style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">The Odyssey</em>, consider where you have encountered the hero’s journey in&nbsp;<span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">a story that you have read or movie you have seen</span>. In a 7 paneled&nbsp;<strong style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">ZINE</strong>, retell a story that you know in words and pictures, labeling seven or more steps from the 12-step hero’s journey model. Then, answer the ECR question about fate and free will in the tale of the Cyclops on the back of the page.</li>\n<li style=\"margin:0px;\">After learning about the hero's journey, and reading \"The Cyclops\" from&nbsp;<em style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">The Odyssey</em>,&nbsp;<span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">retell the story of Odysseus's mini hero's journey in the tale</span>. In five panels of a&nbsp;<strong style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">COMIC</strong>, recount the story in words and pictures, making sure to label five or more steps from the 12-step hero's journey model. Then, answer the ECR question about fate and free will on the handout.</li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px;padding:0px;line-height:1.4;\" dir=\"ltr\">Paper handouts given in class.&nbsp;<br>Grading for this assignment is up to a 95. 10 extra points can be earned by reciting \"Invictus\" by William Ernest Henley for a total possible grade of 105.</p>",
